WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.283 --> 00:00:13.329
One day a man and his son headed to the market.

2
00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.191
They were leading their donkey along the road.

3
00:00:17.112 --> 00:00:18.713
They planned to sell him at the market.

4
00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:22.996
On their way they passed some farmers.

5
00:00:23.956 --> 00:00:25.818
The farmers burst into laughter.

6
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.422
"They're not even riding their donkey!"

7
00:00:31.902 --> 00:00:32.403
one said.

8
00:00:32.423 --> 00:00:35.745
"That donkey must be useless!"

9
00:00:35.765 --> 00:00:38.808
"Yes," another said.

10
00:00:38.828 --> 00:00:41.830
"How will they ever sell him at the market?"

11
00:00:48.076 --> 00:00:49.176
The father flushed.

12
00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:54.361
please ride our donkey.

13
00:00:55.462 --> 00:00:58.004
Then no one will laugh at our donkey or us."

14
00:01:00.992 --> 00:01:03.494
The son obeyed and climbed up on the donkey's back.

15
00:01:05.316 --> 00:01:07.798
Soon they passed an old woman sitting on a bench.

16
00:01:07.818 --> 00:01:11.881
"How rude!"

17
00:01:12.282 --> 00:01:13.122
she said loudly.

18
00:01:13.142 --> 00:01:17.846
"That boy makes his father walk while he rides on their donkey."

19
00:01:19.247 --> 00:01:20.809
The man felt ashamed again.

20
00:01:25.493 --> 00:01:26.413
get off the donkey.

21
00:01:28.215 --> 00:01:29.076
I'll ride him now."

22
00:01:33.216 --> 00:01:35.138
The man and boy continued on their way.

23
00:01:36.719 --> 00:01:38.600
Before long they passed some girls.

24
00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:42.103
"Look at that terrible father!"

25
00:01:42.723 --> 00:01:43.364
one whispered.

26
00:01:43.384 --> 00:01:47.647
"He's making his son walk!"

27
00:01:49.388 --> 00:01:52.971
"That boy looks so tired," another girl said.

28
00:01:52.991 --> 00:01:56.253
"He should be riding on the donkey!"

29
00:01:58.315 --> 00:01:59.235
The man groaned.

30
00:02:02.876 --> 00:02:04.117
"Son, how about this?

31
00:02:05.218 --> 00:02:06.959
We'll both ride on the donkey."

32
00:02:13.624 --> 00:02:14.864
Soon they saw a couple.

33
00:02:14.884 --> 00:02:17.786
"That poor donkey!"

34
00:02:18.127 --> 00:02:18.847
the wife said.

35
00:02:18.867 --> 00:02:22.890
"Yes!" The husband scowled.

36
00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.431
"How cruel!

37
00:02:25.051 --> 00:02:27.513
Who makes a donkey carry two people at once?"

38
00:02:29.034 --> 00:02:31.456
The father and son climbed off their donkey.

39
00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:34.554
With a sigh, the man looked at their donkey.

40
00:02:34.574 --> 00:02:37.937
"He does look tired."

41
00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:41.039
"What should we do?"

42
00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:42.240
the son asked.

43
00:02:43.261 --> 00:02:44.162
The father thought.

44
00:02:44.182 --> 00:02:47.104
"Let's put the donkey on our shoulders.

45
00:02:47.364 --> 00:02:48.825
We'll carry him to the market."

46
00:02:50.086 --> 00:02:52.508
They carefully tied the donkey's legs together.

47
00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:57.553
"This will make it easier to carry him," the father said.

48
00:02:59.114 --> 00:03:01.255
Then they lifted him onto their shoulders.

49
00:03:05.354 --> 00:03:08.316
As they crossed a bridge, loud laughter rang out.

50
00:03:08.336 --> 00:03:13.038
"Ha-ha! They're carrying a donkey!"

51
00:03:13.478 --> 00:03:14.239
someone yelled.

52
00:03:14.259 --> 00:03:17.421
"What a silly sight!"

53
00:03:17.921 --> 00:03:19.101
another person cried.

54
00:03:22.403 --> 00:03:25.885
The people laughed so loudly, the poor donkey got startled.

55
00:03:27.286 --> 00:03:30.628
He kicked his legs hard and slipped off his owners' shoulders.

56
00:03:31.404 --> 00:03:35.627
With a terrible splash, he fell into the river—and drowned.

57
00:03:36.808 --> 00:03:38.689
The boy burst into sobs.

58
00:03:38.989 --> 00:03:42.712
"Oh no!

59
00:03:43.012 --> 00:03:46.714
Our donkey!"

60
00:03:47.235 --> 00:03:49.356
The father put his arm around the boy.

61
00:03:49.376 --> 00:03:54.379
"My son, remember this always," he said softly.

62
00:03:54.399 --> 00:03:59.623
"When you try to please everybody, you end up pleasing nobody."
